Package: parkeze-display
Version: @VERSION@-@BUILD@
Depends: parkeze-tui
Source: parkeze
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@parkeze.com>
Architecture: all
Description: The console on a Pi's own screen, when it has one.
 Runs the terminal UI on the HDMI console of a board with display output, and
 only when the firmware found a display at boot. With none attached there is
 no framebuffer, nothing drawing to it, and nothing running. For boards with a
 display connector; see PACKAGES_DISPLAY in boards/common/board.conf.
